-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Midnight Resistance
  Publisher   Ocean, 1990
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Midnight Resistance (1990)(Ocean)(128K).z80
  MD5         67bf05d356d51b2b402d88c5f0cdfb21

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: the game keeps its own CPU speed after each sprite update
              instead of being set back to 3.5 MHz; works on NextZXOS v2.10
              (System/Next 26.11).

  Note        Known issues: quiet scenes run about 7% faster than the original
              in JNext (-6.6 to -8.3% in 3 runs), while busy scenes keep its
              pace (-0.4 to +1.8%); the game has no frame limiter of its own,
              so holding quiet scenes to the original's pace needs a pace
              limiter in the hooks, not in this version. Missing: no Enhanced
              colour set; an earlier build ran on a real Next for Dean
              (2026-10-14), but this one, with the loading screen, has not;
              hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite weapons
   3  Infinite backpacks
   4  Infinite keys
   5  Invincible after a death

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

